# Header forms - aim <=50 chars, hard <=72
# |<-------------------------- 50 -------------------------->|< 22 >|
# With a ticket:    JIRA-1: Capitalized imperative subject
# Without:          type(scope): Capitalized imperative subject
# Types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert
# Scope is optional: chore: Update
# Breaking change: add ! before the colon (feat!: ) or footer BREAKING CHANGE:
# Example: feat(ghostty): Add Rose Pine Moon cursor color
# Example: JIRA-1: Handle macOS reattach-to-user-namespace fallback
# Example: chore(ci): Pin ruff v0.9.6 in pre-commit
#
# Body - blank line after subject, wrap at 72
# Explain what and why, not how
# Include context, tradeoffs, alternatives considered, subsystem motivation
# Use imperative mood: "Add", "Fix", "Remove", not "Added"/"Fixes"
# No period at end of subject, capital after colon
# When a ticket exists it is the whole prefix; extra refs go to Refs:/Closes: footers
# For larger changes, explain why the change is correct, what it fixes, how it was tested.

# Footers - blank line before footers, git trailer format
# BREAKING CHANGE: `extends` key now used for extending other configs
# Refs: #123
# Co-authored-by: Name <email>
